# Layers and rotation: Opacity makes a box and all it contains faint, so what lies beneath shows through.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Layers and rotation · Opacity
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: stage
			Box:
				Height: 90
				Background: linear(90, #F6D9A8, #BFDCEB)
		For style: veil
			Box:
				Height: 50
				Background: accent
				Border: 4
				Border color: ink
				Corner radius: 6
	Section:
		Text: Layers and rotation
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Opacity
		Paragraph: `Opacity` paints a box with everything it contains at a percentage from `0%` (nothing is seen) to `100%` (opaque). It goes in an `Image`, a `Frame`, an `Overlay` and a `Page overlay`, and only changes the painting. Each overlay below covers the same two-color stage with a blue box.
			Style: intro
		Stack:
			Gap: 12
			Item:
				Grow: 1
				Base size: 0
				Block:
					Text: Opacity: 100%
						Style: label
					Frame:
						Style: stage
						Overlay:
							Offset: 20 10 auto 10
							Opacity: 100%
							Block:
								Style: veil
			Item:
				Grow: 1
				Base size: 0
				Block:
					Text: Opacity: 60%
						Style: label
					Frame:
						Style: stage
						Overlay:
							Offset: 20 10 auto 10
							Opacity: 60%
							Block:
								Style: veil
			Item:
				Grow: 1
				Base size: 0
				Block:
					Text: Opacity: 25%
						Style: label
					Frame:
						Style: stage
						Overlay:
							Offset: 20 10 auto 10
							Opacity: 25%
							Block:
								Style: veil
		Paragraph: The border and the background of each box fade together, as one thing: the border does not let the background show through. A single faint color needs no Opacity: the color carries it in its last two digits, as in #1B5E8C40.
			Box:
				Margin: 18 0 8 0
		Text: Background: #1B5E8C40
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Overlay:
				Offset: 20 10 auto 10
				Block:
					Style: veil
					Box:
						Background: #1B5E8C40
